            lines {
              text: "      \'Launched in March 1972, Pioneer 10 was humanity\342\200\231s trailblazer to the outer Solar System: the first spacecraft ever to navigate through the Asteroid Belt and the first to fly closely past giant Jupiter. After surviving Jupiter\342\200\231s fierce radiation belts, its trajectory flung it onto an escape path heading toward the red star Aldebaran in the constellation Taurus. NASA heard Pioneer 10\342\200\231s last faint radio beep on January 23, 2003, from 12 billion kilometers away, and the silent probe continues coasting through the dark at 43,000 km/h.\',"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
