              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "      \'After a seven-year journey from Earth, the school-bus-sized Cassini spacecraft entered orbit around Saturn in 2004 and dropped the European Huygens lander onto the hazy moon Titan. For 13 years, Cassini looped through the Saturnian system and discovered towering geysers of salty water spraying out of the icy moon Enceladus. Because Enceladus and Titan might harbor conditions suitable for life, NASA engineers decided not to leave Cassini drifting when its fuel ran low; on September 15, 2017, they steered it to burn up like a meteor inside Saturn\342\200\231s golden clouds.\',"
