  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing UI Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m focusing on building the UI components in a modular and organized way. I\'m starting with `/src/components/StatusStamp.tsx`, aiming for a clear and high-contrast rendering of status stamps with a non-hue-only glyph and accompanying text. The goal is visual clarity for the user.\n\n\n**Refining Globe Interaction**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the globe interaction. I\'ve integrated `globe.gl` and am rendering exhibits at their landing sites. Hover interactions show names and years, both visually and in the HUD, and clicks smoothly fly the view to those markers while opening the exhibit detail panel. I\'m also adding a keyboard accessible exhibit selector strip for improved navigation. Lastly, I\'m integrating a fallback, orthographic globe in case the WebGL context can\'t be established.\n\n\n**Ensuring Full Accessibility**\n\nI\'ve been working to ensure that markers, rotation, zoom, hover tooltips, and click-to-fly functionality all operate flawlessly across all environments, even in headless browsers. In the `/src/components/DeepSpaceView.tsx` component, I\'m displaying Voyager 1, Pioneer 10, and Cassini as an editorial list with an interactive heliocentric distance diagram. This also displays distance from Earth, status stamps, years, and opens the exhibit detail side panel. The exhibit detail panel is designed to be full-screen on mobile and a slide-over side panel on desktop, displaying relevant information.\n\n\n**Developing Exhibit Details**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the exhibit detail panel\'s content. I\'m fleshing out each exhibit\'s information. Each panel now includes a placeholder image, the exhibit\'s story in a few sentences, a section on what we learned from it, a simplified hardware description, a data table, and a source link. I\'m working to make this content engaging and informative.\n\\n\\n\nI\'m also working on a \"Planned vs Reality\" section that compares planned and actual lifespans of the machines, with interactive elements. Finally, I\'m working on a \"Guess the Machine\" quiz with questions based on exhibit stories.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_16504669774328333474"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import React from \'react\';\\nimport { ExhibitStatus } from \'../types\';\\n\\ninterface StatusStampProps {\\n  status: ExhibitStatus;\\n  size?: \'sm\' | \'md\';\\n}\\n\\nexport const StatusStamp: React.FC<StatusStampProps> = ({ status, size = \'md\' }) => {\\n  const getConfig = (s: ExhibitStatus) => {\\n    switch (s) {\\n      case \'STILL WORKING\':\\n        return {\\n          glyph: \'\342\227\217\',\\n          classes: \'border-emerald-500/50 bg-emerald-950/50 text-emerald-300\',\\n        };\\n      case \'SILENT\':\\n        return {\\n          glyph: \'\342\226\240\',\\n          classes: \'border-amber-500/50 bg-amber-950/40 text-amber-300\',\\n        };\\n      case \'ENDED ON PURPOSE\':\\n        return {\\n          glyph: \'\342\227\206\',\\n          classes: \'border-cyan-500/50 bg-cyan-950/40 text-cyan-300\',\\n        };\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const { glyph, classes } = getConfig(status);\\n  const sizeClasses =\\n    size === \'sm\'\\n      ? \'px-2 py-0.5 text-[11px] tracking-wider\'\\n      : \'px-2.5 py-1 text-xs tracking-widest\';\\n\\n  return (\\n    <span\\n      className={`inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-mono font-semibold uppercase border rounded-sm whitespace-nowrap shrink-0 ${sizeClasses} ${classes}`}\\n      aria-label={`Mission status: ${status}`}\\n    >\\n      <span aria-hidden=\\\"true\\\" className=\\\"text-[10px] leading-none\\\">\\n        {glyph}\\n      </span>\\n      <span>{status}</span>\\n    </span>\\n  );\\n};\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create StatusStamp component for STILL WORKING, SILENT, and ENDED ON PURPOSE stamps\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/StatusStamp.tsx\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating StatusStamp component\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create StatusStamp.tsx\"}"
