  planner_response {
    response: "I have built **Abandoned but Not Forgotten**, an interactive 3D museum of NASA hardware left on the Moon, on Mars, and in deep space.\n\n### Key Features Implemented\n\n- **Central Configuration & Exhibit Data**:\n  - `CONFIG` object holds the pinned `globe.gl` URL (`https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/globe.gl@2.35.1/dist/globe.gl.min.js`), replaceable Moon and Mars placeholder surface textures, and default gray placeholder image generators.\n  - `EXHIBITS` array stores all exhibits across the **Moon**, **Mars**, and **Deep Space** with the required schema (`id`, `zone`, `name`, `years`, `status`, `lat`, `lng`, `story`, `learned`, `hardware`, `planned`, `actual`, `source`, `image`).\n- **3D Globe Explorer (`Moon` & `Mars`)**:\n  - Rotatable, zoomable 3D globe powered by `globe.gl@2.35.1`.\n  - Enforces **no atmosphere on the Moon** (`showAtmosphere(false)`) and a thin atmosphere on Mars.\n  - Interactive landing-site markers show the exhibit\'s **name** and **years** on hover, smoothly fly the globe camera to the coordinates when clicked, and open the exhibit side panel.\n- **Deep Space Mode**:\n  - Hides the 3D globe and displays **Voyager 1**, **Pioneer 10**, and **Cassini** in an astronomical distance diagram (in AU and billions of kilometers from Earth) paired with an editorial list showing status stamps (`STILL WORKING`, `SILENT`, `ENDED ON PURPOSE`), distance from Earth, and access to the shared exhibit detail panel.\n- **Exhibit Detail Side Panel**:\n  - Slide-over side panel on desktop and full-screen modal on mobile containing the exhibit\'s name, active years, status stamp, gray placeholder photo, *\"The story\"*, *\"What we learned\"*, *\"Hardware in simple words\"*, a monospace technical data table, and an official NASA mission source link.\n- **Planned vs Reality & Guess the Machine Quiz**:\n  - **Planned vs Reality**: Highlights **Ingenuity** (`planned 5 flights \342\206\222 actual 72 flights`), **Opportunity** (`planned 90 days \342\206\222 actual about 14 years`), and other long-lived hardware from the central data array.\n  - **Guess the machine**: Interactive 5-question multiple-choice quiz with 4 options per question, instant correctness feedback, live score tracking, a final score summary, and a restart option.\n  - Ends with the closing line: *\"These machines were left behind. We have not forgotten them.\"*"
    modified_response: "I have built **Abandoned but Not Forgotten**, an interactive 3D museum of NASA hardware left on the Moon, on Mars, and in deep space.\n\n### Key Features Implemented\n\n- **Central Configuration & Exhibit Data**:\n  - `CONFIG` object holds the pinned `globe.gl` URL (`https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/globe.gl@2.35.1/dist/globe.gl.min.js`), replaceable Moon and Mars placeholder surface textures, and default gray placeholder image generators.\n  - `EXHIBITS` array stores all exhibits across the **Moon**, **Mars**, and **Deep Space** with the required schema (`id`, `zone`, `name`, `years`, `status`, `lat`, `lng`, `story`, `learned`, `hardware`, `planned`, `actual`, `source`, `image`).\n- **3D Globe Explorer (`Moon` & `Mars`)**:\n  - Rotatable, zoomable 3D globe powered by `globe.gl@2.35.1`.\n  - Enforces **no atmosphere on the Moon** (`showAtmosphere(false)`) and a thin atmosphere on Mars.\n  - Interactive landing-site markers show the exhibit\'s **name** and **years** on hover, smoothly fly the globe camera to the coordinates when clicked, and open the exhibit side panel.\n- **Deep Space Mode**:\n  - Hides the 3D globe and displays **Voyager 1**, **Pioneer 10**, and **Cassini** in an astronomical distance diagram (in AU and billions of kilometers from Earth) paired with an editorial list showing status stamps (`STILL WORKING`, `SILENT`, `ENDED ON PURPOSE`), distance from Earth, and access to the shared exhibit detail panel.\n- **Exhibit Detail Side Panel**:\n  - Slide-over side panel on desktop and full-screen modal on mobile containing the exhibit\'s name, active years, status stamp, gray placeholder photo, *\"The story\"*, *\"What we learned\"*, *\"Hardware in simple words\"*, a monospace technical data table, and an official NASA mission source link.\n- **Planned vs Reality & Guess the Machine Quiz**:\n  - **Planned vs Reality**: Highlights **Ingenuity** (`planned 5 flights \342\206\222 actual 72 flights`), **Opportunity** (`planned 90 days \342\206\222 actual about 14 years`), and other long-lived hardware from the central data array.\n  - **Guess the machine**: Interactive 5-question multiple-choice quiz with 4 options per question, instant correctness feedback, live score tracking, a final score summary, and a restart option.\n  - Ends with the closing line: *\"These machines were left behind. We have not forgotten them.\"*"
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    thinking_signature: "\022\367\001\n\364\001\001i\024}\023b\247\305\035|\346\210\307\322\347d\005\304\331\352cW\307\326\3160zVy\\\205\362\306\373\3750\302\321=E\213-\361\334\322RK\300\242\374\316\371-\227\310Zy;\364V\324\245\264\373\315\314\001\373;\v\323k\3133G\343\257\303\025\032\307\350\352\024\202\326\245\303\032%m\355\025\374\343\366\320\331X\217\227+\266\360@slc\373\321\356\324\301y\\ \320\370d\260\234\267\377\267d\t\001\352\260\271\b\005F\025\215\023P\232]h1\240\215\220\313\'Y:E\216J[\236\364\b\256\365\245\254\254\363%.3c>%K*b\307\371\233\251\340\215\354VX\206\337\3514\356\305\226\350\\\002\'d\3239\004\245\026\264\362i\375\300\363\262\335\265\207\240\341G\220\270u\200\247\366\373\223\347\232\235\ab\326\271\371B\v\373\324\300\353\246!\257\2112:i\214/\330U\202\037"
